                            <comment id="15390578" author="sergi.vladykin" created="Sat, 23 Jul 2016 06:40:52 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;The original reported issue is &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-3516&quot; title=&quot;H2 Indexing unregisterCache method does not cleanup resources and causes memory leak with OFFHEAP_TIERED cache mode cache.&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;IGNITE-3516&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;IGNITE-3516&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15391546" author="kromulan" created="Mon, 25 Jul 2016 08:40:30 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;To me it seems that stop() and removeTable already deal with these issues or am I missing something ?&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15391909" author="sboikov" created="Mon, 25 Jul 2016 13:46:21 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Hi Sergi,&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I moved cleanup logic in new method TableDescriptor.onDrop and added some tests. Could you please review? Changes are in branch ignite-3560 (compare with master).&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Thanks&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15393358" author="sergi.vladykin" created="Tue, 26 Jul 2016 07:38:16 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=sboikov&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;sboikov&quot;&gt;sboikov&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I pushed one minor change, otherwise looks good, please merge!&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15393368" author="sboikov" created="Tue, 26 Jul 2016 07:42:43 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Merged into master (commit #44cabd8).&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15393369" author="sergi.vladykin" created="Tue, 26 Jul 2016 07:43:02 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=kromulan&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;kromulan&quot;&gt;kromulan&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;You are missing the fact that the same thing was done in 3 different places differently and there were no tests for correct clean up. The error you&apos;ve reported happened because of that. Now we are ok.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15395433" author="kromulan" created="Wed, 27 Jul 2016 10:47:28 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Yes that is true, thanks.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
